<div id="S4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multimodal QA Evaluation on MMHal-Bench.</span>
Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.4 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Causal Decoding for Hallucination-Resistant Multimodal Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows the results on MMHal-Bench. COAD achieves the highest average score (2.52) and the lowest hallucination rate (0.52), significantly outperforming all baselines. The strong performance is consistent across multiple benchmark subsets, particularly in the Attribute, Comparison, and Relation categories, indicating improved factual accuracy and reasoning. These results further demonstrate that incorporating object-level cues effectively reduces hallucination while maintaining or enhancing generation quality.</p>
</div>
